WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.660
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.660
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.730
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.730
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.860
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.860
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.870
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.870
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
Keep your eyes on me, okay!?

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:36.740
My name is Kurata Sana, first year junior high school student.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.070
Hayama... Akito.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:42.080
The amazing white bat Babbit.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.370
Have you ever loved someone?

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:49.630
Matsui Fuka. The friend whom I met in the bathroom with a Kansai accent.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.960
The Two of Them
Finally Bid Goodbye

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:04.560
Yesterday... on TV... Kamura said strange things...

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:10.610
I thought he was talking nonsense at the time...

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:17.490
But I still want to know... the truth from you... I don't know what's going on.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.280
Tell me the truth!

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:27.120
Only from you... I'll only believe the words that you personally say to me!

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.920
The truth...	?

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.340
The truth...

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:44.600
Then Hayama, will you also tell me the truth?

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.020
Do you really love me?

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:54.270
Naozumi-kun told me that you have feelings for me...

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.860
Kamura... what's he doing?

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.360
...like yesterday on TV...

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.490
Naozumi-kun and I are only friends...

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.870
...although we've ended the friendship.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:09.660
On the set, he told me he liked me... but I turned him down...

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:13.000
...because you're the one I like.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.890
Hey, take that thing out.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.100
What "thing"?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.060
That thing that you always take out.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.770
Ah! This?

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:30.980
Lemme have it.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:34.900
Ouch!

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.570
I think I've seen this.
Oh yeah, in a gift shop.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.780
You've gone too far!

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.990
You said you like me, what a joke!

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.870
What?

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.160
I said don't joke around with me!

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.580
Why are you so mad? I only said it because you wanted me to tell you the truth!

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.500
But why all of a sudden?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.880
I only realized it when I was out shooting the film!

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:59.460
You're so stupid and slow...
You never understood my feelings.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.970
How am I supposed to know your feelings?

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.470
That's why I said you're slow!

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.600
I've always loved you!

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.890
But... I just never said it.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.480
Really you feel that way about me...

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.360
If that's true,
why didn't you tell me earlier?!

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.660
How can I say such embarrassing things?

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.490
What? You said it just now!

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.000
Yeah, it just slipped out.
It's embarassing...

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.420
What did you say?!

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.880
How would I have known if you didn't say it!

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.960
If you were normal,
you would've understood.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.670
I'm just not normal!

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.090
Truly abnormal. Different, strange.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:50.100
Implying there is nothing of substance within.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:50.100
Anyway, my brain is as watery as fruit!

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.180
That looks yummy!

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.770
I wasn't talking about that.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:04.780
See ya...

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.530
Hey wait a sec, not done yet...

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.790
That's that.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:15.080
You liking me is in the past.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.880
Now you're in love with Fuka, right?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.880
Hold on, now I...

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.170
Oh, you're still here.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.890
No wonder it was so noisy.
What are you doing?

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:30.680
If you're feeling better, hurry up and return to your classrooms!

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.560
Hurry, hurry, go, go.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.560
Same thing goes to you over there.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.560
Eh? Who?

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.770
Fu... Fuka...

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.610
I thought a sprained finger should be no big deal,

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.990
I was wondering what took you so long so I came here to check on you...

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.740
Fuka! Wait, Fuka!

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.410
That's right.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:59.170
Hayama already has Fuka, I should never have said anything... about the truth...

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:00.790
Never should have said it.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.380
Fuka!

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.170
Sorry, please don't mind what I said, okay?

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.590
How can I not mind?

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.890
The one he loves is you!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.680
Oh no,

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.770
she heard our entire conversation...

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:18.770
You never understood his feelings...

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.190
So why now...

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:23.980
Sorry. Because I thought it didn't matter...

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.070
What did you say?!

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:30.870
...because Hayama's love was already buried in the past. And same with me!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:36.000
I realized that I liked him in the mountains where I was shooting...

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.540
But I've already given that up,
and I'm trying to go on.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.250
It was quick...

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.170
...so it's all in the past.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.590
So, don't worry about it anymore, okay?

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:55.390
That's right, it will be true anyway, but why did I have to blurt everything out? I'm such an idiot.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:58.390
Even if I don't mind, Akito...

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:01.940
Hayama...

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.360
Why are you sneezing at a time like this?

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.570
And you look like Kadocha (a comedic actor).

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.570
I couldn't help it.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.580
I won't break up!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.160
Fuka!

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.100
I can't...

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.390
I can't pull myself together...

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.070
And I can't face either one of them anymore...

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.420
Sana-chan!

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.790
News! News! Excellent news!

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.590
- Rei-kun! Are there more jobs for me to do?
- Sana-chan... a lot of things are coming up!

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.590
- I knew it, there's none!
- But we rejected those.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:16.890
- I'll do anything, and I mean it!
- We had so many chances, that's too bad.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:19.060
Wait a minute. You guys are talking about completely different things at the same time.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.680
Try again, and say it in order!

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.980
Rei-kun, are there more jobs for me?

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.560
Sana-chan, there's a lot of them.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.060
Yea!

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.280
Looks like a real bad talk show, doesn't it?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.610
More jobs! More jobs!

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:33.240
Hey, hey, but why?
What happened to DrePro?

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.990
Does anyone remember?
DrePro stands for Dream Productions.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.530
Babbit's lessons

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:40.580
The group hated Sana-chan,

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:45.460
and tried to prevent Sana-chan from getting jobs. They're very bad people.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:48.590
Actually, DrePro fell apart!

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.380
How? Bankruptcy?

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.880
No, it's not like that.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:56.050
When they tried to interfere with you, a bunch of termites chewed out their building.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.720
Everything else remains alright

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.600
So only their building fell apart.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.760
Hey, is that really true?

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.890
The most idiotic way to end a business in Japan. How great!

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.690
But they weren't great men!

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:07.690
Then at the same time, all these calls came.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:11.980
Soap operas, commercials, talk shows, movies, radio, magazines and others.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.700
Hey, Rei-kun... let's accept all of them.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.580
Really? You're not kidding, right?

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:20.580
I mean it.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:24.080
Sana-chan! Thank you! I'm so proud to be your manager!

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:27.670
Now that it's settled. Better make phone calls right away!

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:28.960
He's floating with joy.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.090
Sana.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:33.380
Mama.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.760
Although I don't know what made you change your mind,

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:39.180
but if you want to do it, don't give up half way.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.600
Sensei!

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.260
Ah! Onda!

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:44.890
What's going on with this draft? It's only half way done!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.270
This only has the first page!

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.400
Ah, I knew it.
You found out almost instantly.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.690
Of course!

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.690
Uh oh. Time to escape!

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.530
- Mama!
- Sensei!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.860
Anyway, it's still better to have some jobs to do.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:00.870
If I totally focus my mind on it, perhaps it'll help me forget.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:04.580
I've always loved you!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:08.580
How can I not mind?
The one he loves is you!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.880
I won't break up!

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.460
I want to be away from those two.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.380
It might be selfish of me...

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:22.100
...but that's my only choice.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:30.100
Principal's Office

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:29.400
The next day, Mama and I had a meeting with the principal.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:32.570
I think it should be fine.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.570
Everything will be fine.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:36.360
Hopefully it will.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.860
A gathering of strange people.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.280
Hey! Sana-chan!

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:41.280
There's a meeting about the new job! Hurry up!

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.490
Okay!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.170
Sana-chan!

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.460
Oh, Tsuyoshi-kun, what's up?

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.800
You just talked with the principal, right?

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.470
Yep. Just some things that needed to be discussed

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:02.890
because I won't have time to come to school in the future.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:06.680
And, I heard that even if I have too much absences, I'll pass the grade if I pass the tests.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.680
You won't come to school again?

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:09.770
Yeah, that's right.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.480
Sana-chan, hurry!
We're gonna be late!

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.060
I'm coming now!

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:16.070
Gotta go, Tsuyoshi-kun.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.490
Sana-chan...

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:22.070
Is that true?

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.660
Yeah, I heard it from Sana-chan before she left.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.160
I'll feel so lonely...

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:32.580
Naozumi! I heard that Sana-chan is going to be officially starting her acting career!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:33.960
Huh? Sana-chan?

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.460
Hmm... Naozumi-kun looks good in this outfit.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:37.170
Is that so?

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.670
But why so suddenly...?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:42.260
Is it because of what happened on TV recently...

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.760
Oh yeah! Why don't I just call?

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.770
But I can't, our friendship is over.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:51.060
Don't worry anymore about the woman who dumped you, okay?

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.270
Hey, but you're the one who told him everything.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:56.570
Kamura-san!
It's time for Rappon no Kyuu-chan.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.190
That's right.
Let's not think about that now.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.280
Naozumi's finally getting it.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:02.860
Did you mean the show?

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.290
This... This is the best way...

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:17.290
What is iageno?

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.880
It means Onegai (please).

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:39.480
Since then, Sana never came back.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.780
I know it's probably all my fault.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:46.370
We haven't discussed this topic...

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:52.290
It's what that girl decided. Forget about it.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.670
So you don't care at all?

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:58.250
Yeah.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.170
Then, I should do the same.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:02.170
Yeah.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:14.690
Hayama!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.060
Let's have a party, Hayama!

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.570
You wanna go visit the cemetery?

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:22.860
Nope! It's called the "half-birthday party" - very popular among girls!

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.990
It's on Christmas Eve!

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:31.790
Christmas party! A party with lots of girls and boys! I've decided we'll exchange gifts!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.000
Hayama, you like dinosaurs, right?

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:43.630
Sweet dreams... sweet dreams...

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:47.130
Aa-chan, it's mother.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:53.520
Aa-chan, I love you, so you have to do your best...

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.360
Do my words mean nothing to you?

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.490
Do you... want to be my real boyfriend?

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.370
That won't work. Be strong.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:21.460
Let me help you do somersaults! Plus huge spins too!

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.590
I've always dreamed of having a dog.

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:25.670
But I can't have any in an apartment...

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:28.090
...so its name is "inu"(dog).

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:37.310
You're smiling! That's good!

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:41.310
Be strong... be strong.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.280
Hi, Hayama.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.370
Did you just have Karate practice? You're working pretty hard.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:57.290
Well, I want to apologize for last time... I said strange things.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:02.380
We won't be seeing each other much in the future, so I came to say goodbye.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:06.050
I'm going to concentrate on my acting career.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:10.970
And I'm sure that I'll find a good man soon.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:14.970
Really, you're in the past.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.890
Past?

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:20.690
That's right, in the past.

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:26.070
So please tell Fuka to forget about it all. I'm sorry.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:27.860
I...

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:28.860
Hmm?

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:35.030
I just can't drop Fuka like that.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:39.750
Of course.
It goes without saying, Hayama.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:47.670
Well, I have to go. Stay strong!

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.270
Hayama...

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:12.280
If only time could stop...

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.870
I don't want any past or future...

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.280
...just this moment...

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:19.370
I just want to stay like this forever!

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.290
But I...

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:33.880
Bye-bye...

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.600
Hayama.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:24.770
After that, Sana-chan...

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:29.060
Sana-chan is seriously engaged in a tight schedule of

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:33.360
soap operas, commercials, radio, movie, and comedy talk shows.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.990
She's no longer a child actress nor an idol.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:37.990
Sana-chan!

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:39.870
Okay, I'll be right there!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.370
She finally looks more cheerful.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:45.870
This schedule looks like one that a super star uses.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.670
Sana-chan, I'm so happy!

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.090
Crying, Rei-kun?

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.380
Man tears.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:56.090
Hey, Sana-chan! I heard that Sana-chan is very very popular!

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.390
What are you doing?

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:01.680
Especially that movie, the critics say it's very good.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:09.350
Ah... I've got it. It's called Mimizu (Earthworm) Palace.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.480
Huh? Mimizu?

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:15.780
Zenjiro-sensei, that's wrong, it's not Mimizu Palace. It's called Mizu (water) Palace, Mizu!

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:16.860
To promote it, it's going to be advertised that...

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:20.570
...during the premiere of "Water Palace", I'm going to go onstage and say hi to my fans!

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.660
What's wrong, Zenjiro sensei?

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:24.790
That hurts!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:25.790
Let's begin the class.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.000
Sana-chan is so mean.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.880
Your outfit disturbs other people.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:34.460
Hurry up! Need to make it to the next call! Hurry! Hurry!

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.470
Ah! It's Naozumi-kun.
Don't stop all of a sudden, okay Sana-chan?

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.760
It's Sana-chan!

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:43.760
Oh yeah, she's cut off our friendship.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.060
I feel so weak.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.270
Hey, Naozumi.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:51.690
The breakup is over! The breakup is over! The breakup is over!

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:52.480
Sana-chan!

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.780
About that... the thing that you said on TV...

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:58.990
...ended up being a good thing for me.

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:00.070
Eh?

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:03.280
Since I couldn't stand seeing the two of them together...

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:08.790
I was thinking, maybe it wasn't so bad after all.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.170
That means, we're still friends!

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.380
U-kih-so-ro-y

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.960
Same here... u-kih-so-ro-y

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.300
Yoroshiku (pleased to meet you)

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:19.380
Ah... This week's Sana-chan!

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:21.970
It's good to make up, right Naozumi-kun?

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:24.680
This kid can really sleep!

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.850
That's how children grow.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:29.890
Don't you think he's gotten bigger lately?

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:32.060
There's an old Chinese saying that says "every time you sleep you gain an inch".

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:34.690
Akito-kun, come on...

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.190
So, you're finally awake!

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:41.700
Don't you want to learn my lessons?

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:43.370
Not at all.

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:44.370
What?!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:45.990
Get the hell out!

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:50.290
Akito-kun, anything can be settled. Come on, please apologize.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.790
Stop this attitude of yours,
come on, Akito-kun...

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.590
There's nothing we can do about you, Hayama...

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:56.670
That hurts!

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.970
Come on, Akito-kun, you can't act like you did today again.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:06.180
You're the one who was dozing off.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:10.680
That jerk focuses on me. It makes me angry.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:13.190
But it's your attitude that caused the problem, right?

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.190
...but Sengoku-sensei is a bit scary, too.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:19.860
Don't worry about the things in the past, okay?

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:22.860
Look, look up there!

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:24.990
It's Sana-chan.

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.580
Wow... Sana-chan looks so beautiful...

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:32.870
Is Sana-chan really that beautiful?

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:35.380
Efforts of the make-up artist and photographer.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.960
Hayama-kun, that's mean!

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:42.090
But Sana-chan is so amazing lately. She's constantly on TV.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:45.300
Somehow she feels so distant...

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:46.760
Sana...

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:50.270
Hey, Fuka-chan... does Sana-chan still come to school sometimes?

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:54.900
Mmm. Yeah. But even if she comes she's always almost late.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:56.690
And leaves about 2 or 3 hours later.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:58.690
So I don't get to talk to her much.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:02.690
Really? That means we probably won't see much of her in the future.

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:04.360
Our classrooms are far apart too, and...

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:04.990
Tsuyoshi...

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:06.200
What?

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.160
Stop talking about her!

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:11.870
Akito...

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.420
Ah! Akito, wait a moment.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:24.340
Hey, don't you think the two of them are acting a little strange lately?

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:26.590
There's something we don't know, right?

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:29.760
Just now, Akito-kun's glare looked frightening...

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:31.680
Just like a long time ago.

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:35.690
- There's something strange...
- That's impossible, right?

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.270
Babbit knows.

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:41.690
